<title>SPAIN: Spain spending to rise 1.7 pct in 1997.</title>
<headline>Spain spending to rise 1.7 pct in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish government's 1997 budget draft contemplates a rise in expenditure of 1.7 percent, Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato said on Friday.  </p>
<p>&quot;This assumes a very important difference between forecast spending increases and inflation forecasts,&quot; Rato said.</p>
<p>This will not affect social spending and will pave the way for lower inflation and interest rates, Rato added.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
